## 3. Dependency-graph resolution from package manifests

Parse project manifests into a canonical dependency subgraph — one node per package
(keyed by name), with `depends_on` edges to declared dependencies. Cover, at minimum:
`pyproject.toml` (via `tomllib`/`tomli`), `pom.xml` (via `defusedxml.ElementTree` to
avoid XML entity-expansion issues), `go.mod` (a small deterministic line-based parser —
no mature Python parser exists for this format), `package.json` (stdlib `json`), and
`Cargo.toml` including workspace members (`tomllib`/`tomli`). A manifest that fails to
parse must be skipped with a logged warning, never abort the whole extraction run. Cap
manifest file size before parsing. Versions that don't parse cleanly (git refs, path
deps, wildcards) should still produce a node, flagged `unresolved_version`, rather than
being dropped or crashing.

