## 4. Blast-radius / indirect call resolution

Extend "what's affected by changing X" analysis to catch indirect references, not just
direct calls:
- Reflective/dynamic dispatch (e.g. `getattr(obj, "name")`-style lookups).
- A function bound to a variable name, returned from a factory function, or re-aliased.
- Dispatch tables / handler registries (a function used as a dict/list *value*).
- Callbacks passed by reference into another function call (thread/executor targets,
  map-style higher-order calls, event-handler registration).

Each of these should be resolved per file, independently — one file's AST-walk failure
must not stop extraction of the rest of the corpus. Scope name resolution correctly to
avoid false positives (a shadowed local name must never bind to an unrelated global
callable of the same name) and cap resolution fan-out to avoid pathological blowups on
very large registries.

